From 6d1a9ff5d89f1d64dad083cd1823e26a3497dc08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:03:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] select: set origin and specificity before cascading the
 inline style

css_select_style() cascades a node's inline style without setting
state.current_origin or state.current_specificity. Those are assigned only
while walking a sheet (select_from_sheet(), match_selector_chain()), so
css__outranks_existing() compared the inline declarations against whatever
the last selector matched from the last sheet left behind, and the inline
style won or lost by accident.

A universal selector leaves specificity 0 behind. So given a class (or id)
rule in one sheet and a `* { box-sizing: border-box }` rule in a later sheet,
the class rule beats the element's inline style:

  sheet 1:  .box { background-color: #e5e5e5 }
  sheet 2:  * { box-sizing: border-box }
  <span class="box" style="background: #333">

renders #e5e5e5. It takes the two rules in separate sheets, the `*`
sheet last, and at least one declaration in the `*` rule. slashdot.org
is such a page: its "This Day on Slashdot" comment-count bubbles lose
their inline background.

CSS Cascade 4 6.4.4 puts the inline style above the author origin's normal
declarations whatever their specificity, so set CSS_ORIGIN_AUTHOR and
UINT32_MAX explicitly. Importance is compared first and is unaffected: an
important rule still beats a normal inline declaration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
---
 src/select/select.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/select/select.c b/src/select/select.c
index faea445..9e4e384 100644
--- a/src/select/select.c
+++ b/src/select/select.c
@@ -1399,6 +1399,11 @@ css_error css_select_style(css_select_ctx *ctx, void *node,
 			state.computed = state.results->styles[
 					CSS_PSEUDO_ELEMENT_NONE];
 
+			/* The inline style outranks every author rule of the
+			 * same importance (CSS Cascade 4 6.4.4). */
+			state.current_origin = CSS_ORIGIN_AUTHOR;
+			state.current_specificity = UINT32_MAX;
+
 			error = cascade_style(sel->style, &state);
 			if (error != CSS_OK)
 				goto cleanup;
-- 
